<h2>How a tap-to-pay sale works in your shop</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Turn it on once.</strong> Activate a tier below and switch on PayPal Tap to Pay in your phone's PayPal app — about five minutes, no reader to buy, charge, or lose.</li>
  <li><strong>Ring up like always.</strong> When the piece is done, enter the total and hold out your phone. The client taps their card, phone, or watch; deposits and tips ride the same tap.</li>
  <li><strong>The money is PayPal's rail, the fee is known.</strong> PayPal takes 2.29% + 9&cent; per tap and the rest is yours. If you turn on the optional register pass-through, half a percent lands on the client's bill instead — about 50&cent; on a $100 tattoo.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Questions shops ask us</h2>
<p><strong>Do I need a card reader or a terminal?</strong><br>
No. Your phone is the terminal — that is the whole point. If your phone can run the PayPal app and take a tap, it can take the payment.</p>
<p><strong>Is this part of my Tattoo Art Customs shop subscription?</strong><br>
No — tap-to-pay is a standalone service with its own monthly tier (Solo, Studio, or Shop, by chairs), billed separately from your shop subscription. Keep the tap-to-pay bill current and the service stays on; the two never hold each other hostage.</p>
<p><strong>What does my shop get beyond the tap?</strong><br>
A listed shop on Tattoo Art Customs gets a referral link that pays 20% on every verified sale it refers, plus a public listing with your location, hours, and appointment requirements. The full picture is on the <a href="/membership/shops">shop membership</a> page and in our <a href="/guides/for-tattoo-shops">guide for tattoo shops</a>.</p>

<p>
  <a class="btn" href="/signup"><%= t('tappay.cta_listed') %></a>
  <a class="btn secondary" href="/membership/shops"><%= t('tappay.cta_earn') %></a>
</p>
